         <component>
            <section ID="id_link_5f583222-cd10-110a-e063-6294a90ae304">
               <id root="5f583222-cd0f-110a-e063-6294a90ae304"/>
               <code code="34067-9" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="INDICATIONS &amp; USAGE SECTION"/>
               <text>
                  <paragraph>• Do not use in large amounts, especially on raw surfaces or blistered areas, wounds, broken or irritated skin; or if you are allergic to any ingredient in this product. • When using this product: Avoid contact with eyes. If contact occurs, rinse thoroughly with water. • Stop use and consult a doctor if the condition worsens, symptoms persist for more than 7 days, symptoms clear up and recur within a few days, or if rash, itching, redness, swelling, irritation, or a burning sensation occurs. • If pregnant or breastfeeding, ask a health professional before use. • Keep out of reach of children. • If swallowed, get medical help or contact a Poison Control Center immediately.</paragraph>
               </text>
               <effectiveTime value="20261103"/>
            </section>
         </component>
         <component>
            <section ID="id_link_5f583347-8d0b-1395-e063-6294a90a3d3a">
               <id root="5f583347-8d0a-1395-e063-6294a90a3d3a"/>
               <code code="34068-7" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="DOSAGE &amp; ADMINISTRATION SECTION"/>
               <text>
                  <paragraph>Adults and children 12 years of age and older: Apply a thin layer to the affected area. Use no more than 3 to 4 times daily. Allow the cream to dry before dressing. Wash hands after use unless treating the hands. Avoid contact with eyes and mouth. • Children under 12 years of age: Consult a doctor before use.</paragraph>
               </text>
               <effectiveTime value="20261103"/>
            </section>
         </component>
